[KiCad-IOS port] FindwxWidgets: do not corrupt paths containing "-I"

Upstream bug, hit for real by this port: FindwxWidgets extracts the
wx include directories from `wx-config --cxxflags` and then strips the
"-I" prefix with a global string(REPLACE "-I" "" ...). That replaces
EVERY occurrence of the two characters "-I" in the whole string --
including inside directory names. Any checkout path containing "-I"
(e.g. a repository named "KiCad-IOS", so every CI path reads
.../work/KiCad-IOS/KiCad-IOS/...) is mangled to "KiCadOS", the paths
stop existing, and configure dies with
"wxWidgets wx/version.h file not found in .../KiCadOS/...".

Fix: strip "-I" only where it starts a list element (the element
separator is ";"). Behaviour is identical for all previously working
paths.

Modified file (GPL-3.0-or-later, same license as upstream):
  cmake/FindwxWidgets.cmake

--- a/cmake/FindwxWidgets.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindwxWidgets.cmake
@@ -841,7 +841,13 @@
           wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS "${wxWidgets_CXX_FLAGS}")
         string(REGEX REPLACE "-I[^;]+;" ""
           wxWidgets_CXX_FLAGS "${wxWidgets_CXX_FLAGS}")
-        string(REPLACE "-I" ""
+        # [KiCad-IOS port] Strip "-I" only at the start of each list
+        # element. A global REPLACE also eats "-I" inside directory
+        # names (e.g. a "KiCad-IOS" checkout path), corrupting them.
+        string(PREPEND wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS ";")
+        string(REPLACE ";-I" ";"
+          wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS "${wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS}")
+        string(REGEX REPLACE "^;" ""
           wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS "${wxWidgets_INCLUDE_DIRS}")
 
         # Flags are a string, not a list, fix it here
